    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with tall reflective posts on both sides so it remains visible at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the driveway so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Maintain vertical clearance along the full length of the driveway to allow passage of fire apparatus and ambulances.\n• Clear a turnaround area near the main residence large enough for a fire engine to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark or designate a flat, firm staging area near the residence where responders can park and work without blocking the driveway.\n• Thin dense vegetation along the driveway to reduce the risk of fire spreading from vegetation to vehicles or structures during an emergency.\n• Keep the path between the main residence and the detached structure clear so responders can move between the two buildings on foot.\n• Post a property map or site diagram at the driveway entrance showing the location of the residence, detached structure, and any gates or barriers along the drive.\n• If a gate is present at the driveway entrance, install a Knox Box or provide emergency responders with keypad access so entry is not delayed."
  },
