    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches and shrubs that are directly touching or overhanging the house and any other structures on the property.\n• Thin the tree cluster visible near the structures to create open space between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the structures.\n• Cut grass short around the structures and along the driveway, especially in the open terrain areas where dry grass can carry fire quickly.\n• Clear brush from the areas immediately surrounding the structures where brush growth is concentrated.\n• Separate shrubs and small trees in mixed vegetation areas near the structures so fire cannot easily move from one plant to the next toward the house.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from the brush areas closest to the structures.\n• Maintain the open areas that already exist between vegetation and structures — do not allow new shrub or brush growth to fill those gaps.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate from the road, supporting access along the single entry route.\n• Thin scattered trees on the sides of the driveway where branches hang low or vegetation crowds the travel lane.\n• Keep grass along the driveway edges cut short for the full length of the drive."
  },
